            <ArticleTitle>Arthroscopic removal of os centrale carpi causing wrist pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>537-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The os centrale carpi is a relatively rare accessory carpal bone of the wrist that infrequently has been reported to cause symptoms. This report describes 2 cases where an apparently mobile os centrale carpi caused painful clicking and crepitus and where the symptoms disappeared after arthroscopic removal of the ossicles.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
